    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0666" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/314: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-31T15:00:00+02:00">January 31, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 31—10:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. The Foreign Office notified this Legation this morning of the intention of
                    the Government to expel Insull at the termination of his <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >permit de séjour</hi> which expires tonight and asked that he be furnished
                        <pb facs="0667" n="567" xml:id="pg567"/> with a valid passport to effect
                    this expulsion. I therefore request immediate revalidation of his passport
                    according to your telegram No. 58, November 22, 3 p.m.<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d463-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
